# Research Style

When editing `fpl_analytics/research.py`, keep the module docstring contract. Recalibrate after each GW. Facts first, implication second. No slogans, no second-person imperatives (`do not`, `keep`, `start`).

## Role Vocabulary

Use only: selected, omitted, retained, sold, ineligible, blocked by club cap, insufficient sample.

## Templates

**Strategy** — two to four declarative sentences.

**Squad note** — `GW{n}: {min} min; {events}; {pts} pts. GW{n+1}: {venue} {opp}. {role}.`

**Watch / sold** — `{club}, £{price}. {sample}. {constraint}.`

```
# BAD
"Home to Coventry. Start. Retain."
"Fade Hull after one result."
"Do not spend the second free transfer on Hull."

# GOOD
"GW3: 90 min; CS, 2 BP; 8 pts. GW4: A MUN. Selected. Retained as the City defender."
"Hull assets are away at Chelsea; one-week residuals are not treated as rates."
"No free transfer remains after Semenyo → Ødegaard."
```
